{"archetypes":[{"name":"release-flow","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff changes /release sequencing, recovery behavior, temp-note handoff, and post-publish cleanup with several cross-step invariants.","prompt_body":"Investigate whether the updated /release instructions preserve the intended ordering across prepare, notes composition, confirmation, PR merge, publish/promote, upgrade, and cleanup. Pay close attention to variable lifetime across separate Bash fences, recovery instructions after partial Step 6 failures, dry-run exits, and whether cleanup can accidentally run before a release is safely published. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"shell-contracts","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff relies on precise Bash helper contracts, ff-only git behavior, nonfatal cleanup envelopes, and test instrumentation.","prompt_body":"Review the local-cleanup shell script and regression harness for contract mismatches introduced by switching to git pull --ff-only and by wrapping git in the tests. Check bash portability, set -e interactions, trap/output-envelope behavior, argument-safety cases, and whether the tests accurately prove no merge-capable pull shape is used. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
